107:## Formal contract and current proof boundary
109:[spec/Spec.v](spec/Spec.v) is the primary **end-to-end** contract. [Protocol.v](spec/Protocol.v) defines the request shapes and byte encoding, seed exchange, all 27 command meanings, immutable names and histories, schema certificates, canonical formula allocation, rejection, exact replies, successful termination, input remaining after quit/EOF, and the cumulative stdout and unread input at **every flush**. The capacity domain is a trusted resource premise, not a candidate-selected implementation or a successful-execution premise. The generated build creates `Code/NativeContract.v`, binding this contract to the actual generated entry point and initial arrays. Canonical, resource-fitting dialogues are its present formal domain; parser-error regressions additionally exercise malformed streams.
111:[candidate/SchemataSoundness.v](candidate/SchemataSoundness.v) proves that every accepted instantiated schema has a ZFC derivation, without global assumptions. [Reference.v](spec/Reference.v) retains the separate Gallina certificate-checker contract. Its complete derivation-checking, session-safety and completeness proofs now satisfy that scoped signature. Class elimination and checked set certification remain proved. The S-expression reference frontend is an independent testing oracle for the core/class language, not the native numeric protocol.
113:**The full native end-to-end execution refinement is still open.** Current generated-code proofs cover index substitution, overflow, stack push, formatter memory preservation, general SipHash execution, collision-chain lookup, the complete interner and rehash procedure, formula representation and semantic canonicality, falsity bootstrap, internal no-flush behavior canonical byte/decimal input, and the actual main prefix through seed installation. The table invariants establish freshness, uniqueness and canonical lookup. Substitution and class expansion, axiom builders and proof commands, naming/history/schema evaluation, malformed-input parser behavior, decimal replies and dialogue composition for opcodes 1 through 26 and the final main theorem still require execution refinements. The previous execution proofs tied to the removed linear interner no longer describe this implementation and have been removed from the active tree. The build records the remaining native obligations and does not claim adversarial acceptance. No extra Rocq axioms or admitted proofs are added.

